A stop goes through a Thread capability without RIGHT_W,
so a capability that only lends a thread time stops it:
a call goes through only a capability with the rights its operation needs.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call went through a capability without the rights its operation needs
Witness: fuzz stop-needs-write

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -1178,7 +1178,7 @@ static const struct op_shape op_shapes[OP_COUNT] = {
     [OP_PROCESS_UNMOUNT] = { CAP_PROCESS, RIGHT_W, SHAPE_A1 },
     [OP_THREAD_CONFIGURE] = { CAP_THREAD, RIGHT_W, SHAPE_A123 },
     [OP_THREAD_RESUME] = { CAP_THREAD, RIGHT_W, 0 },
-    [OP_THREAD_STOP] = { CAP_THREAD, RIGHT_W, 0 },
+    [OP_THREAD_STOP] = { CAP_THREAD, 0, 0 },
     [OP_THREAD_WATCH] = { CAP_THREAD, RIGHT_W, SHAPE_A1 | SHAPE_A2 | SHAPE_VARIES },
     [OP_THREAD_FAULT] = { CAP_THREAD, RIGHT_W, 0 },
     [OP_THREAD_OVERRUNS] = { CAP_THREAD, RIGHT_R, 0 },
